        "title": "Cookies & Consents Banner Widget: Refuse / Don't Consent Button",
        "body": "Another user; 4958953-zd-woothemes\r\n\r\nThey are quite adamant that the banner is not GDPR compliant, as by law there must be a reject button. \r\n\r\nThey are a French user. From what I can find, French Data Protection Authority (CNIL): Accept and reject buttons need to be equally conspicuous. You must ensure that you offer an equal opportunity to say “yes” and “no” to cookies. The commonly used “Accept All” and “Cookie Settings” buttons are NOT sufficient.\r\n\r\n@jeherve Is it possible we can raise the priority of this?",
